  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1055 PM CDT Sun Jul 19 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will be squarely overhead Tuesday with even \nstronger heating in the lower atmosphere. High temperatures will \nreach their peak Tuesday, with widespread upper 90s to low 100s. \nHeat indices of 105-113 F are expected. An Excessive Heat Watch \nwas issued for the areas which will be the hottest. A weak cold \nfront will then move in Tuesday night into Wednesday morning. This\ncold front is expected to be dry, but will at least knock \ntemperatures down a few degrees.\n\nThe upper level ridge will remain in control, but will shift \nslightly west by Friday. At the surface this will do nothing for \ntemperatures, with highs actually expected to increase back to the \nupper 90s to low 100s. But the shift may allow for a few showers and \nstorms to return to northwest AR. By Saturday, the ridge will \nhave shifted far enough west for a weak shortwave trough to clip \nthe area. Models have become more confident in this outcome over \nthe last day, with rain chances also increasing. With that said, \nthere is still considerable uncertainty in the exact placement and\ntiming of the trough as well as any precipitation chances. \nTemperatures are expected to come down at least a little bit by \nnext Sunday.",
